-data><parties><applicants><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGASHINO KOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>KYOTO DAIICHI KAGAKU KK</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGASHINO, KOUJI</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>KYOTO DAIICHI KAGAKU CO., LTD.</name></addressbook></applicant><applicant status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></applicant></applicants><inventors><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>HIGASHINO KOUJI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="epo"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA SATOSHI</name><address><country>JP</country></address></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>HIGASHINO, KOUJI</name></addressbook></inventor><inventor status="new" format="intermediate"><addressbook><name>NISHIMURA, SATOSHI</name></addressbook></inventor></inventors></parties></bibliographic-data><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="EN"><p>A blood test tool with which blood in a dry state can be held without denaturation. In the blood test tool wherein a card made of filter paper is impregnated with the blood and then the blood is held in a dry state, a carboxylic acid such as citric acid is added to the part for holding the blood. Thus, the carboxylic acid exerts an effect of preventing the blood in the dry state from denaturation. It is preferable to add a non-reducing sugar (sucrose, etc.), an anticoagulant (EDTA, etc.) and an antioxidant (glutathione, etc.) together with the carboxylic acid. This blood test tool can be produced by impregnating a filter paper card with a solution containing citric acid, etc. dissolved therein and then air-drying.</p></abstract><abstract load-source="docdb" source="national office" status="new" lang="FR"><p>L'invention concerne un dispositif d'analyse sanguine à l'aide duquel on peut conserver du sang à l'état sec, sans que celui-ci soit dénaturé. On a ajouté à ce dispositif, comportant une carte de papier filtre imprégnée de sang, sang que l'on maintient ensuite à l'état sec, un acide carboxylique tel que de l'acide citrique au niveau de la partie destinée à retenir le sang. Ainsi, l'acide carboxylique exerce une action consistant à empêcher le sang, à l'état sec, de se dénaturer. Il est préférable d'ajouter un sucre non réducteur (sucrose, etc.), un anticoagulant (EDTA, etc.) ainsi qu'un antioxydant (glutathione, etc.) en même temps que l'acide carboxylique. On peut produire ce dispositif d'analyse sanguine en imprégnant une carte de papier filtre à l'aide d'une solution contenant de l'acide citrique, etc., dissoute dans cette carte, puis en séchant le dispositif avec de l'air.</p></abstract><copyright>User acknowledges that the Information Retrieval Facility (IRF) and its third party providers retain all right, title and interest in and to this xml under applicable copyright laws. User acquires no ownership rights to this xml including but not limited to its format. User hereby accepts the terms and conditions of the Licence Agreement set forth at http://www.ir-facility.org/legal/marec/data_licence</copyright></patent-document>